  "fixture_kind": "original_oracle_cards",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Unlike other creature types in Magic that are each only one word, the two words \"Time Lord\" represent a single creature subtype. Time Lord is the only two-word creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "2a73db99-5e31-49a8-91e7-b28b3434585d",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect instructs you to choose a creature type, you may choose Time Lord.",
      "oracle_id": "2a73db99-5e31-49a8-91e7-b28b3434585d",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Neither \"Time\" nor \"Lord\" are creature types. Some older cards were printed with the subtype \"Lord,\" but all of those cards have updated Oracle card text that removed that type.",
      "oracle_id": "2a73db99-5e31-49a8-91e7-b28b3434585d",
      "published_at": "2023-10-13",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Food is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some creatures, it's never a creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "2a73db99-5e31-49a8-91e7-b28b3434585d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whatever you do, don't eat the delicious cards.",
      "oracle_id": "2a73db99-5e31-49a8-91e7-b28b3434585d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Food to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Food token to activate its own ability and also to activate Maraleaf Rider's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "2a73db99-5e31-49a8-91e7-b28b3434585d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whatever you do, don't eat the delicious cards.",
      "oracle_id": "a68e57f3-f138-4c26-b8d5-55d1adec44a8",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Food is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some creatures, it's never a creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "a68e57f3-f138-4c26-b8d5-55d1adec44a8",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Food to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Food token to activate its own ability and also to activate Maraleaf Rider's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "a68e57f3-f138-4c26-b8d5-55d1adec44a8",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some triggered abilities trigger \"whenever you sacrifice a Blood token.\" These abilities trigger regardless of why you sacrificed that Blood token.",
      "oracle_id": "a68e57f3-f138-4c26-b8d5-55d1adec44a8",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Blood token to pay multiple costs.",
      "oracle_id": "a68e57f3-f138-4c26-b8d5-55d1adec44a8",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect refers to a Blood token, it means any artifact token with the subtype Blood, even if it has gained other subtypes.",
      "oracle_id": "a68e57f3-f138-4c26-b8d5-55d1adec44a8",
      "published_at": "2025-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Food to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Food token to activate its own ability and also to activate Maraleaf Rider's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "ab8d5f5c-1976-4f77-8ed2-8d28ee666741",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Food is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some creatures, it's never a creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "ab8d5f5c-1976-4f77-8ed2-8d28ee666741",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whatever you do, don't eat the delicious cards.",
      "oracle_id": "ab8d5f5c-1976-4f77-8ed2-8d28ee666741",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn\u2019t provide any additional benefit.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it\u2019s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don\u2019t grant bonuses to your opponents\u2019 Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed.",
      "oracle_id": "e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
